CONTEXT Migration INCLUDES Kurk FROM "existing.adl" AS old,
                           Kurk FROM "desired.adl" AS new
CONTEXT Migration IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Migration
{+ The migration system of the proof of concept in
"Data Migration under a Changing Schema in Ampersand" (RAMiCS 2024), written as a context
that includes the existing system as `old` and the desired system as `new`.
The numbers of the steps refer to section 4.1 of that paper. +}

-- Step 1. The data sets of both systems are present, kept apart by the aliases.
-- Every atom of the existing system is an atom of the desired system.
CLASSIFY old.A ISA new.A
CLASSIFY old.B ISA new.B

-- Step 2. Copy the population of r. The relation copyR registers what has been copied,
-- so that a user can change a copied pair in new.r without it being copied again.
RELATION copyR[old.A*old.B]
ENFORCE copyDone : copyR >: new.r /\ old.r
ENFORCE copy : new.r >: old.r - copyR

-- Steps 3 to 5. The desired system has a new blocking invariant: r is total.
-- The data of the existing system violates it, so the migration system relaxes it.
-- Step 3: the relation fixedTotalR holds the atoms that satisfy the rule,
-- and the blocking invariant blockTotalR keeps a violation that has been fixed from recurring.
RELATION fixedTotalR[new.A*new.A]
RULE blockTotalR : fixedTotalR |- new.r;new.r~
MESSAGE "Relation r[A*B] must remain total."
VIOLATION (TXT "Atom ", SRC I, TXT " must remain paired with an atom from B.")
-- Step 4: a transactional invariant registers every atom that satisfies the rule.
ENFORCE fixTotalR : fixedTotalR >: I[new.A] /\ new.r;new.r~
-- Step 5: the rule itself is a business constraint here, which signals what users have to repair.
-- In the desired system, where no role maintains it, the same rule is a blocking invariant.
ROLE User MAINTAINS new.totalR

-- The screen of the desired system, so that a user of the migration system works as in the desired system.
INTERFACE Kurk FOR User : "_SESSION";V[SESSION*new.A] CRuD BOX<TABLE>
  [ "A" : I cRud
  , "B" : new.r CRUD
  ]

-- The two systems side by side, as in figure 4 of the paper.
INTERFACE Migration FOR User : "_SESSION";V[SESSION*old.A] cRud BOX<TABLE>
  [ "A" : I cRud
  , "old r" : old.r cRud
  , "new r" : new.r CRUD
  ]

ENDCONTEXT
